 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission's baseRevisionId matches the visit's current head revision, the system SHALL accept it as the next sequential revision.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission's baseRevisionId is an ancestor of the current head revision but not the head, the system SHALL accept it as a competing revision attached to the same visit.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a submission's baseRevisionId is not present in the visit's revision history, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a visit has competing revisions, the system SHALL return status "competing" with the competing revisions array and SHALL NOT include the visit in export-eligible results.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a visit has no competing revisions, the system SHALL return status "clean" with the head revision and SHALL include the visit in export-eligible results.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a coordinator resolves competing revisions, the system SHALL create a new resolved revision that becomes the visit's head, record the coordinator identity and contributing revision IDs, and mark the visit status "resolved".
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a submission references a plot ID not present in the site catalog, the system SHALL reject the submission.
